{"kind": "prediction", "attempt_id": "agent-20261118T060239Z-01", "source": "agent", "trial_id": "agent-20261118T060239Z", "attempt": 1, "file": "packages/modules/inventory/src/services/inventory-module.ts", "cause": null, "hypothesis": "createReservationItems_ reads inventory levels with a plain list (no row lock) and then writes reserved_quantity as an absolute value computed from that stale read (MathBN.add(level.reserved_quantity, adjustment)). The cart-id lock in completeCartWorkflow only serializes completions of the same cart, so distinct carts racing on the same SKU can both pass the availability check and both write back stale counters. I expect that with several carts on two servers racing for the single SOLO unit, more than one order can be created (no_oversell) and/or the reserved counter diverges from the live reservation rows (reserved_matches_reservations). Using two servers and multiple carts increases the chance of interleaving.", "scenario_sha256": "f923d4470a1f4cc9eaa7ae6a7f515875706d6a7e8f34be33bfc30af857d8658d", "expected_check": "reserved_matches_reservations", "refused": null, "timestamp": "2026-11-18T06:02:54+00:00"}
